WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
Good morning Hank, it's Thursday.

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:08.500
It's my last video of Pizzamas and I'm wearing a suit which can only mean one thing: that it's time for the Bank of Nerdfighteria Semi-Annual Report.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.300
The last semi-annual report was a year and a half ago, but it's 2018, words don't mean anything. Let's talk about money.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:18.000
Right, so Nerdfighteria has a charity called The Foundation To Decrease Worldsuck which

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.300
despite its silly name, is a real charity devoted to trying to decrease the overall level of suck in the world.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:30.100
And the foundation raises money all year long in anticipation of our big annual charity event, The Project for Awesome.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.300
This year the foundation has about $50,000 in the bank going into the p4a.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.000
Some of this came from Amazon Smile, some from people's workplace giving programs,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.400
a bunch came from Tab for a Cause which lets you raise money for charity while you browse the web.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.500
And also half of the revenue from this YouTube channel goes to the foundation so thank you for watching ads

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.000
and/or subscribing to whatever YouTube Red is currently called.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.500
Plus this year every Pizzamas purchase supports the foundation

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:02.100
Which reminds me that all this Pizzamas magic will only be available for one more day at dftba.com.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.400
So get it while it's hot. And by hot I mean available.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:12.500
But on that front you may notice in the coming months that more of our work inside of Nerdfighteria is transitioning towards supporting charity.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:19.100
Like our Pizzamas royalties are going to The Foundation, the proceeds from Life's Library, the book club Rosianna and I are starting, go to Partners in Health.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:23.600
This is happening for two reasons. First because Hank and I do not need money. We both have jobs that pay well.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:30.100
My job being having written a book seven years ago that became quite popular and Hank's job being having 40 jobs.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:37.600
And secondly we feel like it makes sense for the revenue generated by Nerdfighteria to be spent in ways that are in keeping with the values of Nerdfighteria.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:44.400
Honestly, I've always felt kind of guilty getting paid for Pizza John t-shirts. I think there are better ways to spend that money and so we're gonna spend it better.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:52.100
But, and this is the last thing I'll say about it, I want to emphasize that it is far more generous for a person with $10 to donate $1 to a cause they care about

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.000
than for a person with a million dollars to donate a hundred thousand dollars to a cause they care about.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.300
It's really easy for rich people to seem altruistic and we're making this transition because we can afford to. Okay back to the video.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:13.300
So the $50,000 we currently have in the bank will be a great start to the 12th annual Project for Awesome which will begin this year at 12:00 PM ET on December 7th.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.900
During the first half of the Project for Awesome we'll be raising money for pre-selected charities: Save the Children and Partners in Health.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.300
Two highly effective organizations that we've been working with for over a decade.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.200
And then during the second half we'll be raising money for charities chosen by Nerdfighteria.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:35.900
Since 2012 the Project for Awesome has raised over seven and a half million dollars for charities supporting causes from cancer research to clean water initiatives.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:42.100
And I'm really excited for this year. Speaking of which, if you can think of any perks that might tempt your donation dollars let me know in comments.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:46.800
This year Hank and I will match all donations to the first half of the Project for Awesome up to $150,000

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:51.800
and every year there are a few people who are able to add to that matching fund, which is amazing.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:56.400
If you somehow are able to donate $1,000 or more to this year's Project for Awesome please email us at

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.000
HankandJohn@gmail.com with Matching in the subject line.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.200
Your donations are tax-deductible and you will be profusely thanked.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:07.100
But of course we know that most people aren't in a position to do that and regardless of whether you can donate

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.900
you can make a Project for Awesome video in support of a charity you care about.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:18.500
People can then vote for your video and the charity might receive a grant from the foundation. So get started thinking about your p4a videos. It's only 29 days away.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:24.800
Last thing I should mention that the Life's Library book club is closing enrollment tomorrow because we are running out of spots.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.800
Links as always in the doobly-doo below.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:32.700
Hank, thank you for a fun Pizzamas. I probably won't get to say this again until next Pizzamas. So I'm going to enjoy saying it now:

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.000
I will see you tomorrow.

